Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-18 (CC0 1.0: no rights
reserved, the full text in LICENSE), no third-party content: every symbol and
footprint is drawn here, under KiCad's library names (Device:R, Device:C,
Connector_Generic:Conn_01x02, Regulator_Linear:AMS1117-3.3, power:+5V,
power:+3V3, power:GND, power:PWR_FLAG; Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric,
Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric, Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-223-3_TabPin2,
Connector_PinHeader_2.54mm:PinHeader_1x02_P2.54mm_Vertical) so an Update
the board finds KiCad's own footprints. For the design blocks units (wave 2
plan, projects and content, I-FIX-BLOCKS; ledger rows DB1 to DB3).

The project, two sheets:
- blocks-small.kicad_sch (Root): J1, a two pin header, giving +5V and GND,
  each with a PWR_FLAG, and the sheet Load (load.kicad_sch);
- load.kicad_sch (Load): R1, 1k, from +5V to GND;
- blocks-small.kicad_pcb: J1 and R1 routed on F.Cu inside a 15 by 10 mm
  Edge.Cuts rectangle;
- design-block-lib-table: one row, blocks-small_blocks, type KiCad, uri
  ${KIPRJMOD}/blocks-small_blocks.kicad_blocks;
- the project file turns off the library comparisons (lib_symbol_issues,
  lib_symbol_mismatch, lib_footprint_issues, lib_footprint_mismatch), as the
  symbols and footprints are our own drawings.

The design block library blocks-small_blocks.kicad_blocks, one folder per
block holding <name>.kicad_sch, <name>.json (description, keywords, fields)
and, for a block with a layout, <name>.kicad_pcb:
- LDO: U1 AMS1117-3.3 (SOT-223), C1 10u on its input (+5V), C2 22u on its
  output (+3V3), GND; schematic and layout, the layout placed and routed
  (0.5 mm tracks on F.Cu), no board outline (a block's layout carries none);
- LDO_PARTIAL: the same schematic (U1, C1, C2), its layout without C2 and
  C2's two tracks: the layout lacks one footprint the schematic names, for
  the failure row of Apply block layouts;
- RC: R1 10k from the hierarchical label IN to OUT, C1 100n from OUT to GND;
  schematic only.

What kicad-cli 10.0.4 (the kicad/kicad:10.0.4 image) reports, measured
2026-11-18; no file has a parse error:
- sch erc blocks-small.kicad_sch: 0 violations (both sheets);
- pcb drc --schematic-parity blocks-small.kicad_pcb: 0 violations, 0
  unconnected items, 0 schematic parity issues;
- pcb drc LDO.kicad_pcb: 4 violations, 0 unconnected items: invalid_outline
  (no Edge.Cuts, by design) and lib_footprint_mismatch for U1, C1 and C2 (no
  project file beside a block, so KiCad's defaults compare our drawings with
  its library);
- pcb drc LDO_PARTIAL.kicad_pcb: 3 violations, 0 unconnected items:
  invalid_outline and lib_footprint_mismatch for U1 and C1;
- sch erc on a block alone (not asked by the recipe): LDO and LDO_PARTIAL 10
  each (power_pin_not_driven on +5V and GND, no PWR_FLAG in a block, and 8
  lib_symbol_mismatch), RC 6 (IN and OUT have no parent sheet, IN meets one
  pin, power_pin_not_driven on GND, 2 lib_symbol_mismatch).

files.json lists the files the e2e harness opens (the project and every
block file). The KiCad files carry no comment (their formats have none), so
this file holds their license.
